ob-like '*/config.py', without the disambiguating path prefix given to the reconciler boundaries; multiple config.py modules exist (src/rebar/config.py, llm/config.py, review_bot/config.py, opcert_service/config.py, _engine/rebar_reconciler/config.py) and the adapters live under src/rebar/llm/, so the exact seam path set is under-specified.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3f2108ade6562e8b","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Outcome → 'Approved seams (two DISTINCT sets) + owner-registry derivation' → Composition roots bullet","norm_id":"na5b0416b9f184033","priority":0.099,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer must hand-write the seam-membership predicate and cannot tell whether '*/config.py' means every config.py in the tree or a specific subset, nor which directory 'anthropic_model.py' resolves to"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Replace the bare filenames with repo-relative paths and enumerate (or precisely define the match rule for) the config.py composition roots.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that cats 1/2/5 site-level diagnostics (path/symbol/access-kind) and receiver-alias detection come from the gate's own AST walk (scan() only supplies name-level baseline/owner mapping), and reconcile that scan()'s _is_os_environ does not recognize receiver-aliased reads so the baseline-owner map may under-count a credential's readers.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.4139,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["gen_env_registry.scan() signature returns tuple[dict[str,set[str]], list[tuple[str,int,str]]] — literal reads carry no lineno/access-kind (scripts/gen_env_registry.py:70-129)","_is_os_environ only matches Attribute(attr='environ', value=Name('os')); `src.get('JIRA_API_TOKEN')` has func.value=Name('src') and is NOT recognized (scripts/gen_env_registry.py:60-67, 96-100)","access_check.py:75 `\"jira_api_token\": src.get(\"JIRA_API_TOKEN\", \"\")` — the very read the plan cites in step 2 is invisible to scan()","Plan step 4 requires per-finding `symbol` and `access kind`, which scan()'s name->module mapping does not carry"],"finding":"The reused gen_env_registry.scan() returns only name->{module-path} for literal reads (plus a separate dynamic list) with no per-site lineno or access-kind, and its _is_os_environ matcher matches only the literal os.environ chain — so it cannot see receiver-aliased reads (e.g. access_check.py:75 `src.get('JIRA_API_TOKEN')`). The plan's required diagnostic (path/symbol/access-kind/owning-seam) for cats 1/2/5 and its receiver-alias detection therefore cannot be produced from scan()'s output; they demand an independent AST re-walk the plan does not spell out, and the 'declared-env baseline <- scan' derivation will under-map which module reads a credential.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe20ada1c13464461","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 1 ('Import scan/... directly'), step 2 (receiver aliasing), step 4 (Diagnostic), and 'Declared-env baseline <- gen_env_registry.scan'","norm_id":"na7194ba2af543383","priority":0.1861,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The gate needs to emit `path:lineno symbol access-kind` for a below-seam os.environ.get read but only has scan()'s name->module set","A credential is read only via a receiver alias below a seam; scan() never surfaces it, so neither the cat-5 check nor the baseline-owner mapping sees it"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Clarify in step 1/step 4 that the gate performs its own per-module AST walk (reusing _is_os_environ/_str_literal/KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS as matchers) to produce lineno/symbol/access-kind and to apply the step-2 receiver-alias resolution, and use scan() only for the declared-env name baseline — noting that scan() itself will not list the aliased reader.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Mitigate the coupling to gen_env_registry's underscore-prefixed helpers (`_is_os_environ`/`_str_literal`) — either add a self-test asserting those symbols remain importable/behave as expected, or note a lightweight stability contract so a gen_env_registry refactor cannot silently break the gate.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T5e"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["\"Import scan/KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS/_is_os_environ/_str_literal directly from gen_env_registry.py (single source; no shared-module extraction)\"","Compatibility only guards one direction: \"Importing gen_env_registry.py's scanner leaves its --check output unchanged\" — nothing guards the gate against gen_env_registry internal churn."],"finding":"The gate imports private, underscore-prefixed internals of gen_env_registry.py (`_is_os_environ`, `_str_literal`) creating a cross-module coupling with no stability boundary; a future refactor of gen_env_registry could silently break the gate.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb0148074bd20f3cc","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 1 / Compatibility","norm_id":"n1673985504dd29aa","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["gen_env_registry.py renames or changes the signature of `_is_os_environ`/`_str_literal` during unrelated maintenance, breaking the gate silently."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a self-test that imports the reused symbols and asserts their presence/behavior on a known fixture, so a gen_env_registry refactor fails the gate's own test suite rather than silently regressing detection.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","pre